{"availability":"available","full":"cgrtml/neural-trees","name":"neural-trees","description":"sklearn-compatible PyTorch implementations of Soft Decision Trees, HMoE, and classifier comparison tests (5×2cv F-test). pip install neural-trees","category":"Education","language":"Python","stars":38,"forks":6,"created":"2026-04-11T20:41:54Z","updated":"2026-10-03T02:03:19Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pypi.org/project/neural-trees/","topics":["decision-trees","deep-learning","machine-learning","mixture-of-experts","python","pytorch","sklearn","soft-decision-trees","statistical-tests"],"demo":"https://neural-trees.streamlit.app/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:53.042Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:53.042Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:53.042Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-07T13:35:53.042Z","stars":38,"forks":6}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Soft decision trees, mixture of experts, and statistical model comparison tests for Python. A scikit-learn compatible library implementing classic machine learning algorithms from research papers, with a PyTorch backend.","Decision boundary learning with Soft Decision Trees on a toy dataset.","An auditable model package. cases/german-credit is a complete example on the public German Credit data: a soft tree measured against logistic regression, CART, random forest, XGBoost and LightGBM on identical folds with the dataset's cost matrix, then calibration, the rules, three explained decisions with counterfactuals a real applicant could reach, slices by age, sex and residency, refit stability, and the JSON and ONNX model files with an agreement check, all written into a model document from the numbers. Result: the soft tree ties logistic regression on accuracy, AUC and cost and adds…"],"features":["scikit-learn compatible API (fit, predict, score, works in Pipeline)","PyTorch backend with GPU support (device=\"auto\" picks CUDA, then Apple silicon MPS, then CPU)","Torch imported lazily, so the numpy-only half of the library works without it","Soft Decision Trees (classifier and regressor), Hierarchical Mixture of Experts, Multivariate and Omnivariate Trees, GAL","explain(): per-prediction explanations with the path taken, the gates on it and a verified counterfactual"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cgrtml/neural-trees/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f1090a1c8503a5d592362a670a465952d348fa8e50006ff3a99d1c0a1a1eb7a7","extractedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:53.161Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:53.161Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Soft decision trees, mixture of experts, and statistical model comparison tests for Python. A scikit-learn compatible library implementing classic machine learning algorithms from research papers, with a PyTorch backend.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cgrtml/neural-trees/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"f1090a1c8503a5d592362a670a465952d348fa8e50006ff3a99d1c0a1a1eb7a7","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cgrtml/neural-trees/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:53.162Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-03T02:03:19Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/cgrtml/neural-trees/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-07T13:35:53.164Z","hash":"f1090a1c8503a5d592362a670a465952d348fa8e50006ff3a99d1c0a1a1eb7a7","originalBytes":23941,"storedBytes":23941,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["soft","tree","decision","test","model","every","trees","alpayd","hard","one","same","against","classifier","library","which","examples","iris","models","rather","train","what","author","cart","import","mixture","split","title","where","year","comparison","depth","gal","journal","open","over","pipeline","python","rows","run","scikit-learn","algorithms","article","benchmarks","combined","data","experts","fit","fixed","neural","rules","weight","x2cv","breast","cancer","d